00:25:42.083 --> 00:26:03.587
ADR-058 Event-source the wallet; ADR-059 PostgreSQL event store with xid-safe projections; ADR-060 Snapshots and period closing; ADR-061 Event versioning and upcasters; ADR-062 Order tracking as rebuildable read models.

400
00:26:04.937 --> 00:26:05.577
1.

401
00:26:05.857 --> 00:26:07.265
Context and Problem.

402
00:26:07.545 --> 00:26:15.417
Wallet balances were a single mutable column, and disputes (why is my credit 0 rupees?) needed log archaeology.

403
00:26:15.697 --> 00:26:23.419
Order tracking projections skipped events under concurrency (§1.1), and the cart was event-sourced without a need.

404
00:26:23.699 --> 00:26:24.403
2.

405
00:26:24.683 --> 00:26:26.027
Goals or Non-Goals.

406
00:26:26.307 --> 00:26:41.433
Goals: every wallet balance is explainable event by event; no overdraft under concurrency; projections never skip events; read models rebuildable without downtime; event formats can evolve safely; PII erasable.

407
00:26:42.783 --> 00:26:50.420
Non-goals: event-sourcing orders or carts (tables + outbox suffice); a global event store for all services.

408
00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:51.447
3.

409
00:26:51.727 --> 00:26:52.687
Requirements.

410
00:26:54.037 --> 00:26:55.381
Here is a quick table:

411
00:26:55.661 --> 00:26:57.133
ID, and Requirement.

412
00:26:57.413 --> 00:26:58.458
NFR-1:

413
00:26:58.738 --> 00:27:05.949
Wallet invariant balance ≥ 0 holds under any concurrency (0 violations in tests).

414
00:27:06.229 --> 00:27:07.274
NFR-2:

415
00:27:07.554 --> 00:27:12.269
Wallet load p99 at most 20 ms regardless of history length.

416
00:27:12.549 --> 00:27:13.615
NFR-3:

417
00:27:13.895 --> 00:27:15.303
Projection completeness:

418
00:27:15.583 --> 00:27:21.087
0 missed events (checked by a nightly count or sum reconciliation against the store).

419
00:27:21.367 --> 00:27:22.455
NFR-4:

420
00:27:22.735 --> 00:27:28.901
Projection lag p99 at most 2 s; read-your-writes available via min-version queries.

421
00:27:29.181 --> 00:27:30.226
NFR-5:

422
00:27:30.506 --> 00:27:36.351
A full rebuild of order tracking completes in at most 1 h and switches over with no read downtime.

423
00:27:36.631 --> 00:27:37.719
NFR-6:

424
00:27:37.999 --> 00:27:45.082
Every stored event carries type, schema version, correlation or causation ids and an HLC timestamp.

425
00:27:46.432 --> 00:27:47.136
4.

426
00:27:47.416 --> 00:27:49.507
Capacity and latency estimates.

427
00:27:50.857 --> 00:27:52.201
Here is a quick table:

428
00:27:52.481 --> 00:27:54.785
Item, and Calculation, and Result.

429
00:27:55.065 --> 00:27:56.046
Wallet events.

430
00:27:56.326 --> 00:28:01.339
Calculation: ~120 K debits or credits per day at P90.

431
00:28:01.619 --> 00:28:07.977
Result: ~44 M per year, ~1 KB each, then ~44 GB per year.

432
00:28:08.257 --> 00:28:09.409
Longest streams.

433
00:28:09.689 --> 00:28:10.755
Calculation:

434
00:28:11.035 --> 00:28:14.193
B2B wallets: ~300 events per day.

435
00:28:14.473 --> 00:28:19.763
Result: ~110 K per year, then snapshots + yearly period closing.

436
00:28:20.043 --> 00:28:20.982
Load time.

437
00:28:21.262 --> 00:28:22.329
Calculation:

438
