439
00:28:23.763 --> 00:28:29.673
200 K events 180 ms full versus 3.4 ms with snapshot.

440
00:28:29.953 --> 00:28:30.763
Result:

441
00:28:31.043 --> 00:28:33.198
Snapshot every 1,000 events.

442
00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:34.907
Order tracking rebuild.

443
00:28:35.187 --> 00:28:46.579
Calculation: ~1.3 K events per second peak, ~40 M events per month kept 3 months; L3 rate ~22 K events per second single-threaded.

444
00:28:46.859 --> 00:28:54.966
Result: ~1.5 h single projector, then partition by order hash, 4 workers, then ~25 min.

445
00:28:55.246 --> 00:28:56.185
Contention.

446
00:28:56.465 --> 00:28:57.531
Calculation:

447
00:28:57.811 --> 00:29:01.715
One wallet: at most a few concurrent debits (checkout + refund).

448
00:29:01.995 --> 00:29:02.806
Result:

449
00:29:03.086 --> 00:29:07.630
Retry on conflict is fine (L2 showed the worst case with 16 threads).

450
00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:09.748
5.

451
00:29:10.028 --> 00:29:11.223
Proposed design.

452
00:29:11.503 --> 00:29:30.212
Event store in PostgreSQL: events(globalposition bigserial, txid xid8 default pgcurrentxactid(), streamid, version, type, schemaversion, payload jsonb, metadata jsonb, recordedat). primary key (streamid, version), plus indexes on (txid, globalposition).

453
00:29:30.492 --> 00:29:31.516
Append-only:

454
00:29:31.796 --> 00:29:34.697
UPDATE or DELETE revoked from application roles.

455
00:29:36.047 --> 00:29:44.303
Wallet aggregate: stream per customer wallet, expected-version appends, and idempotency by (stream, command id) in metadata.

456
00:29:44.583 --> 00:29:48.743
A saga step (Ch 13) retries with the same command id.

457
00:29:49.023 --> 00:30:02.634
Projections: a projector framework with a (txid, position) checkpoint below pgsnapshotxmin, read-model update + checkpoint in one transaction, upserts with version guards, and blue or green rebuilds.

458
00:30:02.914 --> 00:30:09.250
Integration events: mapped from domain events through the outbox to Kafka (Ch 13 or 14).

459
00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:12.303
Consumers never read the event store directly.

460
00:30:13.653 --> 00:30:19.755
Snapshots every 1,000 events (async, versioned), and period closing each financial year:

461
00:30:20.035 --> 00:30:25.325
PeriodClosedbalance starts a new stream wallet-cust-42 to 2027.

462
00:30:25.605 --> 00:30:34.544
Versioning: schemaversion per event, an upcaster chain per type with golden tests from production samples, and exact decimal arithmetic only.

463
00:30:34.824 --> 00:30:37.021
PII: events carry customerid only.

464
00:30:37.301 --> 00:30:43.637
Where free text could contain PII (a support note), encrypt it with a per-customer key (crypto-shredding).

465
00:30:43.917 --> 00:30:44.664
