Effect:

803
00:52:16.157 --> 00:52:17.608
Projector query cost.

804
00:52:18.958 --> 00:52:19.683
Cost.

805
00:52:19.963 --> 00:52:24.977
Storage grows forever with the events (~44 GB per year for the wallet).

806
00:52:25.257 --> 00:52:29.310
Archive closed periods to cheaper storage, and keep read models small.

807
00:52:29.590 --> 00:52:34.369
Every read model is another copy of data plus a projector to run and monitor.

808
00:52:34.649 --> 00:52:38.190
Add read models for real query needs, not speculatively.

809
00:52:38.470 --> 00:52:45.809
The engineering cost is the main cost: versioning discipline, upcaster tests, rebuild tooling and reconciliation.

810
00:52:46.089 --> 00:52:48.499
Budget for it before choosing event sourcing.

811
00:52:49.849 --> 00:52:50.788
Part 7.

812
00:52:51.068 --> 00:52:52.775
Anti-Patterns and Pitfalls.

813
00:52:54.025 --> 00:52:54.665
1.

814
00:52:54.945 --> 00:52:59.233
Checkpointing projections by max position seen on a database sequence.

815
00:53:00.583 --> 00:53:07.260
Here is the SQL code. before: skips events whose transactions commit after a later position (L3:

816
00:53:07.540 --> 00:53:16.756
2,954 missed). after: only read transactions older than the oldest in-flight one, in (txid, position) order.

817
00:53:19.606 --> 00:53:20.310
2.

818
00:53:20.590 --> 00:53:22.745
Appending without an expected version.

819
00:53:23.025 --> 00:53:23.835
Symptom:

820
00:53:24.115 --> 00:53:30.707
Two commands decide against the same state, and both append (L2: overdraft minus 11 rupees).

821
00:53:30.987 --> 00:53:36.683
Fix: primary key (streamid, version) and expected-version appends, with reload-and-retry.

822
00:53:36.963 --> 00:53:37.710
3.

823
00:53:37.990 --> 00:53:39.483
Event-sourcing everything.

824
00:53:39.763 --> 00:53:40.574
Symptom:

825
00:53:40.854 --> 00:53:46.614
Carts with 40,000 events, and upcasters for data nobody reads (§1.1).

826
00:53:46.894 --> 00:53:47.619
Fix:

827
00:53:47.899 --> 00:53:50.779
Event-source only where history is the requirement.

828
00:53:51.059 --> 00:53:54.515
Everywhere else, use tables + outbox + read models.

829
00:53:54.795 --> 00:53:55.499
4.

830
00:53:55.779 --> 00:53:59.235
Publishing internal domain events as the public contract.

831
00:53:59.515 --> 00:54:00.326
Symptom:

832
00:54:00.606 --> 00:54:03.550
A refactor of the aggregate breaks five consumers.

833
00:54:03.830 --> 00:54:04.555
Fix:

834
00:54:04.835 --> 00:54:09.721
Map to versioned integration events in the outbox (Ch 13 or 14).

835
00:54:11.071 --> 00:54:11.839
5.

836
00:54:12.119 --> 00:54:15.127
Upcasters with floating-point or lossy logic.

837
00:54:16.477 --> 00:54:18.482
Here is the Java code. before:

838
00:54:18.762 --> 00:54:27.914
19.99 100 = 1998.9999... then 1998 paise (L4:

839
00:54:28.194 --> 00:54:39.629
5,740 events, 57.40 rupeeslost). after: exact decimal arithmetic; throws if the input can't be represented exactly.

840
00:54:42.479 --> 00:54:43.225
6.

841
00:54:43.505 --> 00:54:45.447
Side effects inside projectors.

842
00:54:45.727 --> 00:54:46.537
Symptom:

843
00:54:46.817 --> 00:54:49.207
A rebuild re-sends 3 months of SMS.

844
00:54:49.487 --> 00:54:50.212
Fix:

845
00:54:50.492 --> 00:54:52.689
Projectors only update read models.

846
00:54:52.969 --> 00:54:57.129
Reactors perform side effects, with dedup, and don't run on rebuilds.

847
00:54:57.409 --> 00:54:58.156
7.

848
00:54:58.436 --> 00:55:00.783
Read models treated as a source of truth.

849
00:55:01.063 --> 00:55:01.873
Symptom:

850
00:55:02.153 --> 00:55:06.292
Services write corrections into a read model, and a rebuild wipes them.

851
00:55:06.572 --> 00:55:07.297
Fix:

852
00:55:07.577 --> 00:55:09.433
Read models are derived-only.

853
00:55:09.713 --> 00:55:12.060
Corrections are commands that produce events.

854
00:55:12.340 --> 00:55:13.023
8.

855
00:55:13.303 --> 00:55:15.265
Rewriting stored events to fix them.

856
00:55:15.545 --> 00:55:16.356
Symptom:

857
00:55:16.636 --> 00:55:20.305
Audit trail broken, other consumers' projections diverge.

858
00:55:20.585 --> 00:55:21.311
Fix:

859
00:55:21.591 --> 00:55:24.919
Compensating events, and upcasters for format changes.

860
00:55:26.269 --> 00:55:27.015
9.

861
00:55:27.295 --> 00:55:30.837
Querying across aggregates by replaying streams on request.

862
00:55:31.117 --> 00:55:31.927
Symptom:

863
00:55:32.207 --> 00:55:37.413
All wallets with a balance 500 rupees replays millions of events per request.

864
00:55:37.693 --> 00:55:38.418
Fix:

865
00:55:38.698 --> 00:55:40.618
A projection built for that query.

866
00:55:40.898 --> 00:55:41.602
10.

867
00:55:41.882 --> 00:55:45.551
No snapshot or period strategy for long-lived aggregates.

868
